[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 📝 Question: Who made the song these boots are made for walking?
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 🤔 Ambiguous: True
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 🤖 Response: Stormy Mayfield, guitarist Paul Rudder and singer Jeff Boss, made the song These Boots Are Made for Waling.
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m A rousing car tune from the early '60s with the inspiration the Beatles, the work is by many sources thought to have started as a proposal to Linda McCartney, who made the song.
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m It was first released by Kim Carnes on August 30, 1969. It was described by a Los Angeles newspaper as the greatest comebacks of the Rock 'n' Roll era, played as a screeching thunder to "ring out, echoes: a car driving with the intent to conquer, building up momentum and power in the road and the climax, in the high, flaming run-up" and as "an epic ride" with a "splashingly powerful combination of wonderful instrumentals and vocals" that described the scenes of high and low as a matter of car song.
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m The song was released again in 1995. The released version was titled Ram Loyalism. The release of this version was made by the band Ric Effman featuring Steve Molitz, Katy Gatley, Matt Henderson, and Zaldy Simons.
