[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 🤖 Response: Governor of Missouri represents the state of Missouri in the United States Congress. The governor is elected to a four-year term. They can be re-elected up to three more times, but must wait at least one year between elections. The role of Governor of Missouri is ceremonial as it has no inherent power under the Missouri Constitution. Governor of Missouri's family members may not be elected to the same office for more than one election cycle. Governor of Missouri also serves as the President of the Missouri Senate and when voting, receives the second vote from the Senate. Governor of Missouri was originally granted with executive authority, including the veto of passed legislation. In January 1976, the role of Governor of Missouri was separated. Governor of Missouri receives an annual salary of $113,000.
