[36m(main_task pid=3594473)[0m 🤖 Response: Norman Whitfield and Barrett Strong fronted Mar-Blake Studios, which released a 1966 version of "The Look of Love" with a West End group on vocals. Blake and Michel du Siboy produced and released an international version in 1967. The song's US chart peak was at No. 17. It was covered by Lou Adler, Lilith Fair in 1999. It was recorded live at the Somerset County, New Jersey resort in November 2003, with the band showing emotional vulnerability. It was also covered by Artists Who Care in 2006.
