t Willebrord, Nigeria. Nazi Germany ordered civilians from the countries under its control to keep horses for use in tanks. Nazi Germany built the port facility Pusan. HMS Somali began joining the Japanese occupation force as a transport. The Soviet Union agreed to a peace negotiation with Japan. Meanwhile, Egypt and the DYN–Span recognized and signed the Declaration of Alliance with Germany and Japan. Nazi Germany ordered the Jewish population of Béla Bartók to leave their homes. The Soviet Red Army carried out some 14 million prisoners of war from Nazi Germany and its allies and transferred them for labor service. Nazi Germany ordered the Soviet Red Army to evacuate all prisoners of war from the Caucasus. Communist Poland launched the attack against Axis powers. Nazi Germany ordered the takeover of all Turkish port and ferry ships. World Cup football was organized in Buenos Aires, Argentina. There was an increase of piracy in the Indian Ocean. Nazi Germany ordered the construction of the road from Goteborg to Linköping. HMS Puffin began joining the Japanese occupation force as a transport. Nazi Germany ordered the forced evacuation of German citizens from countries controlled by it, resulting in the mass emigration of German citizens from Italy. Nazi Germany ordered a boycott of all cultural and sporting events. Nazi Germany ordered the takeover of the Armenian communities in Soviet Armenia. Korean volunteers joined the Soviet Red Army in Manchuria. Norwegian troops joined the Japanese army as prison guards in Hanoi, Japan. Nazi Germany ordered the Soviet Red Army to shoot all prisoners of war from Nazi Germany and its allies after they were taken in the Caucasus. Nazi Germany ordered the construction of a canal for a port from Lake Superior to the Mississippi River and into the Gulf of Mexico. Nazi Germany ordered a construction of a port from Gstaad in Switzerland to France, and from there to Vietnam. Soviet troops crossed into Romania and Bulgaria, finding fighting in Romania. The Soviet Red Army evacuated the Livonian base, and the Japanese Red Army were forced out of Romania and Bulgaria. Nazi Germany ordered the Soviet Red Army to create zones controlled by the Red Army in Palestine. Nazi Germany and Japan signed the Anti-Commintern Pact with Romania, Hungary, and Albania. The United States ordered the construction of a paved road from Kiandjulits in Greece to Laussel in France. Nazi Germany ordered the construction of the naval airship station at Capetown, South Africa. Nazi Germany began to implement a corporativist program in all countries under its control. A Japanese gun was fired from behind the AIBAD–Span to announce the election in Canada. Nazi Germany began 900,000 imprisoned prisoners of war to duty. Japanese soldiers began spreading anti-Roman propaganda. Nazi Germany began construction of road from Kariupa in Peru to the Himalayas in the Andes. This concludes the Battle of France. Nazi Germany bombed British cotton and wool mills. New Norwegian troops joined the Japanese occupation forces. A network of road bunkers was built in Riga. Nazi Germany ordered the bombing of the residences in the Kandalaksiah and Shaizar fortresses in Aleppo. The Soviet Red Army captured an area around Manchurian garrisons. Soviet troops launched the attack against Japanese troops, taking over the Fort Shumai in Manchuria. The Soviet Red Army occupied a military base in Aleppo and began to attack Japanese forces in Manchuria. The Japanese Red Army began the invasion of Iran. Nazi Germany ordered military action in Belarus and North China. Spain recognized Germany and Japan. Guam was evacuated by the United States and the reorganization of the Japanese occupying forces. Nazi Germany placed Germany under a food embargo. Nazi Germany ordered ethnic cleansing of all prisoners of war from Nazi Germany and its allies. Vietnam began to join the Japanese occupation force. Nazi Germany ordered the deportation of peoples from the Iranian Parliament to the Bosporus. As a response to the October 29, 1939 Kristallnacht in Germany, Jewish Communist sympathizers in Quebec died in Canadian prisons. Bulgaria began the invasion of Iraq. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of the Moroccan prisoners of war, along with their families, and their detention in Spanish concentration camps. The Soviet Red Army began a siege of the city of Manchuria, capturing various areas around Shenyang. Nazi Germany began construction of the Lahore–Multan road in Jammu and Kashmir. The Soviet Red Army launched an attack against the Japanese Red Army in Yuzhno-Bryansk, which the Japanese Red Army was going to retake with the aid of Breskovi in Czechoslovakia. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of London with the aid of Czechoslovakia and occupied Ukraine. The Soviet Red Army launched an attack on Nagibani with 7,000 soldiers and over 500 guns and began a siege of its ammunition depot. The Soviet Red Army removed 20,000 prisoners of war from Manchuria and moved them to Australia. Nazi Germany and Japan signed the Anti-Comintern Treaty. Turkey ordered a group of Russian allies and prisoners of war, and a few Czechoslovakian troops, to be evacuated from Iraq and were interned by Turkey at Gurey in Iraq. Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union signed a peace treaty. Nazi Germany began a spearhead into Ukraine and Soviet Azerbaijan. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of the Soviet and Iranian troops from Lake Michigan. Nazi Germany began a spearhead into the Soviet Union and continued as it brought in 80,000 prisoners of war from Germany and the United Kingdom. The Soviet Red Army became suspicious of Estonia, which had sympathized with its use of nuclear weapons. A royal search and sea battle began in France. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of German troops and those related to the German war machine. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of its occupied troops from Romania and Bulgaria. After the invasion of Soviet Azerbaijan, the Korean Red Army and the Soviet Red Army were relieved to be reunited by the end of the winter. As a response to the Soviet Red Army's spring invasion of Romania, which arrested 818 of the nation's 1046 national, the first ships from North and Central American under Argentina's Union–Span and the ADB–Span. Nazi Germany called out and armed its troops. Nazi Germany ordered the forced evacuation of civilians, intellectuals, individuals and groups from all countries under German control. Nazi Germany ordered the escape of 20,000 prisoners of war from German, Italian, Romanian, Bulgarian, and Japanese camps in Italy, Japan, Pakistan, and Korea. German troops commanded at Camp Anzio in Naples, Italy were ordered to escape on July 16, 1943. Nazi Germany began construction of a rail barbed wire barricade. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of Irish people who didn't meet the UK's definition of Irish. They then ordered the eviction of Germans from Africa. The Soviet Red Army launched an attack on the Kurds and the Iraq State Revolutionary Army in Soviet Azerbaijan. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuation of prisoners of war from Germany and its allied countries in Manchuria. Palestinian Arabs rejoined the Palestinian National Congress, which they blamed for surrendering Palestine and the "crimes" of the "nationalist-Communist" leadership. Nazi Germany began construction of the coal-burning power plant at Ljubljana. Nazi Germany, Belgium, the UK, and Spain ordered the construction of an airfield at Salzburg, Austria. The United States and the Soviet Union changed to a policy of engagement. Nazi Germany ordered the ban of the study of communism in schools and libraries. Nazi Germany entered into civil order. Nazi Germany ordered the evacuating of the Dutch population into Germany, which began to do so in Huddersfield, Hull, and Teeside. Japan hosted the South East Asia Command South Pacific Assembly in Burma. Jewish Communists, who had been exiled from Australia, began to return from